Conquering Evil With Good
Fully confident that Jehovah will fulfill his purposes, we can safely concentrate all our efforts on the work he has given us to do — preaching “in all the inhabited earth ” the“ good news of the kingdom. ” We know that this Christian activity will provoke the anger of our enemies, for Jesus warned us: “You will be objects of hatred by all the nations on account of my name. ”
Rather than feeling animosity toward our persecutors, we try to enlighten them, realizing that some among them may be acting out of ignorance.
In another letter, Paul stated: “When being reviled, we bless; when being persecuted, we bear up; when being defamed, we entreat. ” — 1 Cor.
What is the best way to conquer evil with good?
