How does God feel when his will is ignored?
As God Almighty, he has the entire universe under his authority.
What has especially distressed Jehovah? Satan’s revolt is still going strong.
The Bible describes one such situation with the words: “How often they would rebel against him in the wilderness, they would make him feel hurt in the desert!
And again and again they would put God to the test, and they pained even the Holy One of Israel. ” The pain that Jehovah feels when his people reject him is certainly great.
Clearly, bad things happen, and Jehovah feels deeply distressed when they do. — Read Isaiah 63: 9, 10.
Yes, despite the reproach that has been heaped on him, Jehovah remains “the happy God. ” — 1 Tim.
When things go wrong, how may we imitate Jehovah? Granted, we cannot compare ourselves to Jehovah when it comes to our ability to solve problems.
How did Hannah display reasonableness?
During one of her visits to Jehovah’s sanctuary, Hannah became “bitter of soul, and she began to pray to Jehovah and to weep greatly. ”
After Hannah poured out her feelings to Jehovah, Eli the high priest approached her and said: “Go in peace, and may the God of Israel grant your petition that you have asked of him. ”
He had an affliction that caused him much distress. He called it “a thorn in the flesh. ”
Whatever its nature, Paul did what he could to remove this affliction, praying to Jehovah for relief.
On the contrary, God’s Word entreats us: “Do not be anxious over anything, but in everything by prayer and supplication along with thanksgiving let your petitions be made known to God. ”
The Bible adds: “And the peace of God that excels all thought will guard your hearts and your mental powers by means of Christ Jesus. ”
Proverbs 24: 10 acknowledges: “Have you shown yourself discouraged in the day of distress?
Another proverb says: “Because of the pain of the heart there is a stricken spirit. ”
What are some activities that can help dispel discouragement and give us a measure of joy?
On the other hand, a positive perspective will help us to focus on aspects of our lives from which we can derive delight and joy.
David wrote: “To do your will, O my God, I have delighted. ”
What assurance from Jehovah brings us joy now? God gives us many reasons to be joyful.
His promise of salvation is indeed a major source of happiness. We know that regardless of what is happening to us now, in the end God will reward those who earnestly seek him.
Name some of God’s gifts that we can enjoy while awaiting future blessings.
While we wait for the wonderful future in store for us, Jehovah’s will is that we enjoy the good things that he gives us. The Bible says: “I have come to know that there is nothing better for than to rejoice and to do good during one’s life; and also that every man should eat and indeed drink and see good for all his hard work.
Being tender, hospitable, and forgiving toward our spiritual brothers and sisters also results in much joy, and it pleases Jehovah. And accomplishing our ministry with a self - sacrificing spirit is truly rewarding.
What will bring us complete relief from adversities, and in the meantime, what gives us comfort? Ultimately, our love for God, obedience to his commandments, and faith in the ransom sacrifice will result in our complete relief from the adversities of imperfect life and lead us to lasting joy.
David wrote: “I will be joyful and rejoice in your loving - kindness, in that you have seen my affliction; you have known about the distresses of my soul. ”
