The foretold “seed ” would crush the serpent’s head, eliminating the cause of rebellion, sickness, and death.
Jehovah progressively revealed who the promised “seed ” would be. God swore to Abraham: “By means of your seed all nations of the earth will certainly bless themselves. ”
David was assured, and prophets later confirmed, that the Messiah would be a descendant of his and would inherit the Davidic throne forever. — 2 Sam.
Jesus ’ Credentials as the Messiah
In what way did Jesus come forth from God’s “woman ”?
God sent forth his Son, his first creation, from His wifelike organization of spirit creatures in heaven to be the promised “seed. ”
Anticipating Messiah’s appearance, some asked about John the Baptizer: “May he perhaps be the Christ? ”
By coming to John in the fall of 29 C.E. to be baptized at 30 years of age, Jesus presented himself as the Messiah right on time.
He then began his eventful ministry, saying: “The appointed time has been fulfilled, and the kingdom of God has drawn near. ” — Mark 1: 14, 15.
Though not having full details, Jesus ’ disciples had what firm conviction?
Nevertheless, when Jesus asked, “Who do you say I am? ”
Peter unhesitatingly answered: “You are the Christ, the Son of the living God. ”
Peter answered similarly when many turned away, stumbled over a teaching. — Read John 6: 68, 69.
Listening to the Messiah
In heaven, God’s only - begotten Son was a mighty spirit person.
He said: “What I teach is not mine, but belongs to him that sent me. ”
Confirming Jesus ’ Messiahship during the transfiguration, Jehovah directed: “Listen to him. ”
Although Jesus had overwhelming credentials proving that he was the Messiah, the vast majority of the first - century Jews did not acclaim him.
Because they had their own preconceived ideas about the Messiah, including that he would be a political messiah who would liberate them from Roman oppression.
Thus, they could not accept the Messiah who fulfilled the prophecies that said he would be despised, avoided by men, meant for pains and for having acquaintance with sickness, and finally killed.
The proud, the rich, and the hypocritical viewed these requirements as too difficult to fulfill.
Jesus foretold that he would be condemned by the chief priests and be impaled by Gentiles, but on the third day, he would rise.
His affirmation before the Sanhedrin that he was “the Christ the Son of God ” was judged to be blasphemy.
By this cruel death, he suffered the “heel ” wound foretold at Genesis 3: 15.
Why the Messiah Had to Die
Second, as Jesus said, “the Son of man came... to give his soul a ransom in exchange for many. ”
This “corresponding ransom ” paid the penalty for sin inherited by Adam’s offspring and made it possible to give everlasting life to all who accept Jesus as God’s means of salvation. — 1 Tim.
After three days in the grave, Christ was resurrected, and for 40 days he appeared to his disciples, proving that he was alive and giving them further instructions.
Then he ascended to heaven to present to Jehovah the value of his precious sacrifice and await the appointed time when his presence as Messianic King would begin.
Completing His Role as the Messiah
Outline Jesus ’ role as the Messiah after his ascension to heaven.
Throughout the centuries since his resurrection, Jesus has faithfully supervised the activities of the Christian congregation over which he has been ruling as King.
Shortly thereafter, he led the holy angels in casting Satan and his demons from heaven. — Rev.
The preaching and teaching work that Jesus began in 29 C.E. is nearing its grand climax.
Soon he will judge all the living. He will then tell sheeplike ones who accept him as Jehovah’s means of salvation to “inherit the kingdom prepared for from the founding of the world. ”
Those who reject Jesus as King will suffer destruction when he leads the heavenly armies against all wickedness. Then Jesus will bind Satan and cast him and his demons into “the abyss. ” — Rev.
What does Jesus accomplish in fulfilling his role as the Messiah, bringing what results for obedient mankind?
His Kingdom rule will lift humans to perfection, including those resurrected from the dead. The Messiah will guide willing humans to “fountains of waters of life, ” enabling obedient mankind to enjoy a peaceful relationship with Jehovah.
Have You Found the Messiah?
What reasons do you have to tell others about the Messiah?
Although his presence as King of God’s Kingdom is invisible, it is obvious from the fulfillment of prophecies. Nevertheless, just like the first - century Jews, most people today ignore the evidence of the Messiah’s presence.
You, though, came to know that Jesus is now reigning as King of God’s Kingdom.
Just like the first - century disciples, you were moved to proclaim: “We have found the Messiah. ” Today, when you talk about the truth, do you highlight Jesus ’ role as the Messiah?
How could people in the first century tell that Jesus was the promised Messiah?
When you talk to others, do you highlight Jesus ’ role as the Messiah?
Cultivate Love That Never Fails
What warning does the Bible give about misguided love?
Though he was associated with Paul, Demas turned to loving what the world offered. The apostle John warned Christians against this very danger.
We face what challenge, giving rise to what questions?
We are no part of this world, though we are still living in it.
It is vital that we not let ourselves be trapped by misguided or perverted love. For whom, therefore, should we cultivate and demonstrate principled love?
What provisions enable us to cultivate love that endures all things and never fails?
How does this course benefit us now and affect our future?
We need answers from God’s standpoint so that we can be guided accordingly. Cultivating Love for Jehovah
How does love for God grow?
Think of a farmer who works hard to prepare the soil and plant the seeds. He expects the seeds to grow.
We must work the good soil of our heart, where the seed of Kingdom truth was sown.
Regularly attending and participating in congregation meetings will also help us increase in knowledge.
We can reflect on all of Jehovah’s creative works and be in awe of his superior wisdom.
The universe also gives proof that Jehovah is the Source of dynamic energy and inexhaustible power. — Isa.
It is expansive and affects us all.
He expressed that love in providing the ransom for mankind’s redemption.
This provision is available to the whole world of mankind, but only those who respond to God’s love and exercise faith in his Son will benefit from it. God’s offering Jesus as a propitiatory sacrifice for our sins ought to stir love within us in return.
That is one reason we bear witness about his name and Kingdom, which benefits others. Doing that out of our heart’s abundance is an evidence that we observe God’s commandments with a pure motive. — Matt.
Our brothers around the globe persevere in observing God’s commandments despite facing apathy and outright rejection of the Kingdom message.
They do not let up in their efforts to accomplish their ministry fully. Likewise, we are moved to share knowledge of God with others as well as to observe all his other commands.
Why We Love Our Lord Jesus Christ
What are some of the things that Jesus endured?
While he was doing his Father’s will, Jesus was hated without cause, persecuted, falsely accused, and reviled. He also suffered other indignities.
In view of what Christ did for us, what is our aim? Jesus ’ course stimulates a response in us.
Being his followers, we should aim to cultivate and keep showing Christlike love so that we will endure in observing his commandment to witness about the Kingdom and make disciples. — Matt.
The love Christ displayed was central to his accomplishing what God has purposed for mankind. And the model Christ left for us to follow closely enables each of us to have a part in that divine purpose.
The context in the verses that follow shows that this was the surpassing way of love. In what sense was it surpassing?
If he had certain outstanding abilities and accomplished great things but did not have love, what would he amount to?
Moved by God’s spirit, he drove home this important point. What a powerful impression he made in getting this across to us!
Focus mainly on the last phrase in verse 7 and the first sentence in verse 8: ‘ Love endures all things.
A young German Witness named Wilhelm well illustrates this. Rather than compromise, he remained loyal when facing death by a Nazi firing squad.
Later, in a Watchtower article, a member of his family wrote: “Through the turmoils of time, as a family we have seen to it that our love for God has always come first. ” Such is the spirit of many brothers presently enduring imprisonment in Armenia, Eritrea, South Korea, and other lands.
Similar results have been experienced in other lands.
When opposition comes upon individual Christians from family members, it is quite different. Stress may be caused by members of the household or immediate relatives.
Did not Jesus foretell that this would take place?
Some have even been ordered out of the home, but they were taken in by kindly Witnesses.
How is the love that endures all things a help to married Christians?
There are many other situations in life that call for the love that endures all things. Within the marriage union, love enables couples to respect Jesus ’ words: “What God has yoked together let no man put apart. ”
When experiencing “tribulation in their flesh, ” married Christians should remind themselves that Jehovah is a key party in their marriage.
His Word says that ‘ love endures all things, ’ and a husband and wife clothed with this quality are fortified to stick to each other and keep their marriage intact. — Col.
Many of our brothers lost their homes or material possessions in those disasters.
Eventually, things that we have faith in will become reality, and therefore the need for faith in them will end.
The yeartext for 2010 will be: ‘ Love endures all things.
