JESUS CHRIST used many illustrations, or parables, to explain different aspects of the Kingdom.
In illustrations about sowing the seed of Kingdom truth, Jesus emphasized the role of a person’s heart condition in accepting the message, as well as the role that Jehovah plays in causing spiritual growth.
Jesus also illustrated the outstanding growth of Kingdom interests here on earth even if that growth is not always at first discernible. Additionally, he highlighted that not all who respond to the Kingdom message are necessarily suitable subjects of that Kingdom. — Matt.
This is often called the parable of the wheat and the weeds and is recorded in Matthew chapter 13. Whereas in another illustration, Jesus tells us that the seed that is sown is “the word of the kingdom, ” in this illustration, he tells us that the fine seed represents something different —“ the sons of the kingdom. ”
The Illustration of the Wheat and the Weeds
This is the illustration: “The kingdom of the heavens has become like a man that sowed fine seed in his field.
How, then, does it come to have weeds? ’
Who is the man who sowed the fine seed in his field?
Jesus, the “Son of man, ” prepared the field for planting during the three and a half years of his earthly ministry.
So the objective in sowing the fine seed was eventually to gather the full number of those who would become joint heirs and rulers with Jesus in his Kingdom.
Jesus tells us that the enemy “is the Devil. ”
This poisonous plant closely resembles wheat in its early stages before it reaches maturity.
These hypocritical Christians who claim to be followers of Christ are really part of the “seed ” of Satan the Devil. — Gen.
When did the weeds start to appear, and how were men “sleeping ” at the time?
When did these weedlike Christians appear?
We find the answer in the apostle Paul’s words to the Ephesian elders: “I know that after my going away oppressive wolves will enter in among you and will not treat the flock with tenderness, and from among you yourselves men will rise and speak twisted things to draw away the disciples after themselves. ”
He went on to admonish those elders to keep awake spiritually. After the apostles, who acted as “a restraint ” against the apostasy, began falling asleep in death, many Christians fell asleep spiritually.
Did some of the wheat turn into weeds?
Regarding this, the apostle Peter tells us: “It is the appointed time for the judgment to start with the house of God. Now if it starts first with us, what will the end be of those who are not obedient to the good news of God? ” — 1 Pet.
But how is the symbolic wheat now being brought into Jehovah’s storehouse?
These harvested ones were either brought into the restored Christian congregation, where they have God’s favor and protection, or they received their heavenly reward.
How long does the judgment last?
The judgment of the individual members of the anointed continues throughout the time of the end.
Who will be collected out from the Kingdom, and how do they cause stumbling and do lawlessness?
