Yes, out of consideration for those under the Law, Jehovah lovingly arranged for a day of rest so that his people might “refresh themselves. ”
Was the Sabbath just a day for relaxation?
No, it was an integral part of the Israelites ’ worship of Jehovah.
It also provided an opportunity for family and friends to get together to reflect on Jehovah’s deeds and to have joyous association.
More important, the Sabbath prophetically pointed forward to a time when true refreshment would come through Christ’s Millennial Reign.
