Do You Know God by Name?
Although he also has many titles, such as “Creator, ”“ Almighty, ” and “Sovereign Lord, ” he has always honored his loyal servants by letting them address him by his personal name. For example, the prophet Moses once began to implore God by saying: “Excuse me, Jehovah. ”
And when the prophet Isaiah addressed God on behalf of the people of Israel, he said: “You, O Jehovah, are our Father. ” Clearly, our heavenly Father invites us to address him by name.
Clearly, knowing God’s name must embrace a wealth of meaning, since it is a key factor in receiving God’s protection.
DOES your name have a particular meaning?
Sometimes Jehovah gave a new name to a person who was to have a new role. The barren wife of Abraham received the name Sarah, meaning “Princess. ”
