Why are we helped to understand Jehovah’s thinking if we examine Jesus ’ activities?
Jesus perfectly imitated his Father in everything he said and did.
Therefore, examining Jesus ’ activities helps us to understand Jehovah’s way of thinking.
Let us, then, examine two Gospel accounts.
As recorded at John 6: 1 - 5, what situation led Jesus to ask Philip a question, and why did Jesus do so?
Imagine the scene.
It was just before the Passover of 32 C.E.
After Jesus healed this multitude and taught them many things, a logistical problem arose.
Why did Jesus ask Philip this question?
Was Jesus worried about what to do?
No. What really was his thinking?
The apostle John, who also was there, explains: “ was saying this to test him, for he himself knew what he was about to do. ” Jesus here tested the spiritual progress of his disciples.
Explain. (b) What will we now consider?
How does gaining insight into Jesus ’ way of thinking help us?
Gaining insight into Jesus ’ way of thinking helps us in understanding passages in the Scriptures that may be difficult to grasp. For example, consider Jehovah’s words to Moses after the Israelites had made a golden calf to worship.
Did Moses really need to correct Jehovah’s thinking?
Would Moses succumb to frustration? Would he take this opportunity to encourage Jehovah to forget about Israel and to make a mighty nation from Moses ’ own descendants?
Because Jehovah was not firmly committed to a certain course of action, the inspired record says that he “began to feel regret. ”
How did Jehovah show great patience in dealing with Abraham’s concerns?
What do we learn from the way that Jehovah dealt with Abraham? From this account, what do we learn about Jehovah’s thinking?
Did Jehovah need Abraham to reason with him in order to make the right decision?
But by means of these questions, Jehovah gave Abraham time to come to grips with the decision and to understand His thinking.
Lessons for Us
