What did Jesus discuss?
Then he gave them an assignment: “Go therefore and make disciples. ” Finally, he gave them warm assurance: “I am with you all the days. ”
But did you note what Jesus did not do?
He did not reprimand his apostles; nor did he use that meeting to question their motives or to deepen their feelings of guilt by referring to their momentary weakness of faith. Instead, Jesus reassured them of his and his Father’s love by entrusting them with a weighty assignment.
In imitation of Jesus, elders today view meetings as opportunities to reassure fellow believers of the unfailing love that Jehovah has for his people. Hence, in their meeting parts, elders focus on their brothers ’ strengths, not on their weaknesses.
